column35:
*Problem (one line):* Mobile2 tests today use NON_IDP auth ({{okdirect}}). NMD and similar plans need IDP login. Mobile 1 already has the PKCE path in {{MobileBaseRequestTest}} — this spike proves it for Mobile2 so dashboard/activity tests can reuse the same JWT pattern.

*Goal:* Document the full IDP login sequence for NMD on QC4 → prove JWT → prove one Mobile2 GET (dashboard) → assess reuse for activity and other endpoints.

*Key references already in repo:*

* {{MobileBaseRequestTest.java}} — PKCE when {{idpEnabled: true}}
* {{MobileServerClient}} — {{/mobilemembersession}}, {{/idptokenexchange}}, {{/mobilememberidptoken}}
* {{user/qc4/nmdirect.json}} — NMD fixture ({{idpEnabled: true}}, not yet in suites)
* Postman: {{Mobile Endpoints (w- IDP Session).postman_collection.json}}

*AC (7 bullets):* Auth path doc → NMD IDP login on QC4 → one Mobile2 GET green → property/fixture checklist → reuse table → blockers in RAID → follow-up Story drafted

